  "notes": "{除草|じょそう} means weeding or removing unwanted plants. A compound of {除|じょ} (remove) + {草|そう} (grass/weeds).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {除草|じょそう}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to weed\n- {除草|じょそう}{剤|ざい}: herbicide, weed killer\n- {除草|じょそう}⟦{作業|さぎょう}→作業：02775_sagyou⟧: weeding work\n- {除草|じょそう}⟦{機|き}→〜機：09843_ki⟧: weed trimmer, mower\n\nUSAGE:\nA practical term used in gardening, agriculture, and property maintenance. Common in spring and summer when weeds grow rapidly.\n\nHOMOPHONES (IMPORTANT):\n- {除草|じょそう}: weeding (this entry)\n- ⟦{助走|じょそう}→助走：15506_josou⟧: run-up, approach run (sports)\n- ⟦{女装|じょそう}→女装：12643_josou⟧: dressing as a woman, cross-dressing\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{草|くさ}むしり→草むしり：08195_kusamushiri⟧: pulling weeds by hand (casual, everyday)\n- ⟦{草刈|くさか}り→草刈り：22813_kusakari⟧: mowing grass/weeds",
